    <string name="lisp_confirm_upload_title">Upload to the controller?</string>
    <string name="lisp_confirm_upload">This stops LispBM, erases the stored code and writes %1$d bytes to flash. The code then starts on every boot. Scripts can drive the motor.</string>
    <string name="lisp_confirm_upload_run">This stops LispBM, erases the stored code, writes %1$d bytes to flash and starts it. It also starts on every boot. Scripts can drive the motor.</string>
    <string name="lisp_confirm_run_title">Start the stored code?</string>
    <string name="lisp_confirm_run">LispBM restarts and runs the code stored on the controller. Scripts can drive the motor.</string>
    <string name="lisp_confirm_stream_title">Stream and run this code?</string>
    <string name="lisp_confirm_stream">The code is evaluated as it arrives (%1$s). Nothing is stored; it is gone after a reboot. Scripts can drive the motor.</string>
    <string name="lisp_confirm_erase_title">Erase the stored code?</string>
    <string name="lisp_confirm_erase">This stops LispBM and erases its code from flash, so nothing runs on the next boot.</string>
    <string name="lisp_confirm_close_title">Close %1$s?</string>
    <string name="lisp_confirm_close">It has changes that haven\'t been saved. They will be lost.</string>
    <string name="lisp_close_discard">Close without saving</string>
    <string name="lisp_confirm_clear_recent_title">Clear recent files?</string>
    <string name="lisp_confirm_clear_recent">The list is cleared; no files are deleted.</string>

    <string name="lisp_imports_folder_title">Where are the imported files?</string>
    <string name="lisp_imports_folder_body">This code imports files. Pick the folder they are in; the paths in the import lines are read relative to it.</string>
    <string name="lisp_pick_folder">Pick folder</string>
    <string name="lisp_save_imports_title">%1$d imported files found</string>
    <string name="lisp_save_imports_body">Save the code and its imports to a folder? Files with the same names are replaced, and the folder becomes the imports folder so the code can be uploaded again.</string>

    <string name="lisp_info_title">Code size</string>
    <string name="lisp_info_body">Size:           %1$d bytes\nAfter reducing: %2$d bytes\nReduce:         %3$s\n\nSizes include all imports. Reducing removes comments, indentation and empty lines from the code and from imports ending in .lbm or .lisp.</string>

